```

Routing map entry: `cofounder: "/api/v1/legal/cofounder/analyze"`

### New function: `cofounderAnalyze(text: string)`

**Output schema:**
```typescript
{
  // Analysis
  risk_flags: Array<{
    clause_type: CofounderClauseType;
    severity: "critical" | "high" | "medium";
    issue: string;           // specific problem found
    clause_text: string;     // the problematic text, or "[MISSING]" if absent
    recommendation: string;  // specific fix referencing the rule
  }>;
  missing_clauses: CofounderClauseType[];   // required clauses not found in text
  blocking_issues: string[];               // must be resolved before signing
  overall_risk: "critical" | "high" | "medium" | "low";
  next_steps: string[];                    // specific, non-generic

  // Draft
  draft_clauses: Array<{
    clause_type: CofounderClauseType;
    title: string;
    draft_text: string;      // ready-to-use clause text with [PLACEHOLDER] markers
    notes: string;           // what the attorney must fill in
  }>;
  schedule_b_template: string;  // deliverables schedule template
  rspa_checklist: string[];     // items that must be in the RSPA
}
```

**System prompt rules (always applied, not just retrieved):**
- 83(b): 30-day window from grant date, paper certified mail, IRS service center, copy to company
- RUO: scope must be explicitly limited to research; clinical/diagnostic use requires FDA clearance
- Equity: each product entity (VetOnco, Longevity, DeepCrispr.ai) needs its own cap table reference
- IP: pre-existing IP carve-out required; CMO medical expertise is not company IP
- Vesting: 5% on signing is an immediate grant — must be in RSPA, not just the agreement
- Entity type: S-Corp vs. non-profit must be resolved before signing — it is a blocking issue

