## Part 3 — Governance Rules

New escalation rules added to `LEGAL_GOVERNANCE_POLICY.escalation_rules`:

```typescript
{ trigger: "83b_window_risk",              reason: "83(b) election window — 30-day IRS deadline from grant date. Missing from agreement." },
{ trigger: "ruo_clinical_risk",            reason: "RUO materials in clinical context — FDA violation risk. Scope must be explicitly limited." },
{ trigger: "equity_no_dilution_protection",reason: "Equity dilution undefined across multi-product structure — 30% may not be protected." },
{ trigger: "ip_broad_assignment",          reason: "Broad IP assignment may capture pre-existing CMO medical IP — carve-out required." },
{ trigger: "incorporation_unresolved",     reason: "Entity type unresolved — S-Corp vs. non-profit affects 83(b) validity and equity structure." },
```

**Detection logic in `governanceEngine.ts`:**
- `83b_window_risk`: text contains equity/vesting/RSPA keywords but no `83(b)` or `83b` reference
- `ruo_clinical_risk`: text contains `RUO` or `research use only` AND (`clinical` or `diagnostic` or `patient`)
- `equity_no_dilution_protection`: equity percentage mentioned but no `dilution` or `anti-dilution` or `fully diluted`
- `ip_broad_assignment`: `all inventions` or `all works` without `prior` or `pre-existing` or `Exhibit A`
- `incorporation_unresolved`: `S-Corp` or `non-profit` or `incorporation` mentioned but entity type not confirmed

