## Explicit Assumptions

1. CMO = Chief Medical Officer. CEO/CTO = other co-founder. Both are co-founders.
2. Company not yet incorporated — entity type unresolved. This is a `blocking_issue`.
3. 30% equity is in the primary entity. VetOnco, Longevity, DeepCrispr.ai are separate products/entities with separate equity pools.
4. RUO = Research Use Only materials (reagents, assays, protocols) the CMO brings or uses.
5. 83(b) election applies to the restricted stock grant (RSPA). 30-day window runs from grant date.
6. "5% upon signing" = immediate vesting at grant. Remaining 25% vests on schedule with cliff. Cliff period not yet defined — `blocking_issue`.
7. Draft clauses use `[PLACEHOLDER]` for specifics the attorney must fill in.
8. No fine-tuning. RAG only. Model weights do not change.
9. UI calls live Render API. No mock data.

